--   Trailing blocks stay near the identity (round six, `aseq_rows`)
-- statement:
--   **Trailing blocks stay near the identity.**
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.J6SegILPreJM1`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem J6Seg.aseq_rows : ∀ (L : List ℕ) (A : ℕ → ℕ → ℤ)
--       (b : ℕ → ℤ) (η : ℝ), L.Nodup → 0 ≤ η → η + (L.length : ℝ) ^ 2 / 2 ^ P ≤ 1 / 2 →
--       (∀ i ∈ L, ∑ k ∈ L.toFinset, |(A i k : ℝ) / 2 ^ P - kd i k| ≤ η) →
--       (∀ i ∈ L, ∀ k ∈ L, ¬ S i k → A i k = 0) → PatOK S L →
--       ∀ r ≤ L.length, ∀ i ∈ L.drop r,
--         ∑ k ∈ (L.drop r).toFinset, |(Aseq P S L A r i k : ℝ) / 2 ^ P - kd i k| ≤ 1 / 2
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** B-line IL, `J` pre-table (B5-J), math part 1: the elimination in index form and its bounds
--
--   * `aseq_rows`: under the near-identity hypotheses of `pivPos_of` (same induction), every
--     trailing block of the pattern elimination `Aseq` stays within `1/2` of the identity in row sums;
--     hence (`aseq_entry`, `aseq_piv`) its entries are `≤ (3/2) 2^P` and its pivots `≥ 2^P/2`;
--   * `Mseq`: the elimination on line indices that only updates the trailing block (`q < i, k`);
--     `Mseq_eq`: on the trailing block it is `Aseq` (`Aseq_last`: one more pivot is one more
--     `stepA`); `Mseq_frz`: entry `(i, k)` is frozen from step `min i k` on. So the final matrix
--     holds `Aseq (min i k) (L i) (L k)` at `(i, k)`.
--
